<title>HONG KONG: Strong earthquake rocks western Indonesia.</title>
<headline>Strong earthquake rocks western Indonesia.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>A strong earthquake measuring 5.6 on the Richter scale hit the southern part of Indonesia's western Sumatra island on Tuesday afternoon, the Royal Hong Kong Observatory said.</p>
<p>The quake was detected at 0602 GMT with its epicentre initially determined to be about 300 km (180 miles) southeast of Padang, it said in a statement. There were no immediate reports of damage or casualties.</p>
